According to a report on January 16, from the end of February to the beginning of March, the main research and development unit of the president's car, the Russian National Institute of Automotive Engineering (NAMI), will deliver 16 vehicles to the Federal Security Service.
According to the report, the "Caravan" project requires a unified modular platform to build three kinds of cars for the country's number one person - extended cars, three vans and minibuses. The budget allocation for the project is 12.4 billion rubles.
According to reports, news of the first domestically produced lengthened sedan for the president since the Soviet Union appeared about five years ago. According to the R&D unit's plan, the new car will be equipped with 800 horsepower engines and armor, weighing 6 tons.
It is reported that the engineering technology team of the German Porsche company participated in the development of power units.
According to TASS reported on January 16, Manturov told reporters that the "carriage" series of cars will be retailed from 2019 onwards, and all kinds of models can be purchased.
The minister said: “Starting next year, all those interested will be able to order, whether bulletproof or luxurious, without any sales restrictions.”
Russia's Ministry of Industry and Trade plans to increase the annual production of the "caravan" series of cars to more than 1,000 vehicles after 2020.
Manturov said: "We are now producing 18 vehicles at full capacity, this year's production is more than 70 vehicles, next year's 200 vehicles, the next year 300 or more."
