According to Beijing time on the 9th, Reuters said that Samsung Electronics released the first set of self-driving car components jointly developed with Harman International on Tuesday, as well as infotainment solutions, which is an important measure for the company to enter the car electronics market.
Samsung Electronics acquired Harman International about a year ago.
At this week’s Consumer Electronics Show (CES) in Las Vegas, Samsung unveiled vehicle cameras with collision warnings, lane shift warnings, and cruise control features, developed in collaboration with Harman.
Samsung plans to start shipping the camera system this year, which is built on technologies such as automatic machine learning and augmented reality.
