According to leaked phone records, Trump pressured Mexico to pay for the border wall.
The Washington Post leaked transcripts of calls between U.S. President Donald Trump and the leaders of Mexico and Australia.
On Jan. 27, during a call to Mexican President Enrique Pena Nieto, Trump urged him to stop publicly saying he would not pay for the proposed border wall.
The President of the United States was reportedly unhappy with his public attack on the wall, and Putrand reportedly said to him: "Don't tell the media."
During the presidential campaign, Trump pledged to build a wall along the U.S. southern border and solemnly announced that Mexico would pay for the project.
Records of calls between him and Australian Prime Minister Malcolm Turnbull have also been released, which shows a tense exchange between them.
Trump told Turnbull that it was “absurd” that the U.S. took on a deal to send refugees to Australia that were “abusible” and “stupid,” that he had advised the U.S. to ban refugee resettlement, and now stick to a deal brokered by the Obama administration that would make him look like a “fool.”
Trump hung up the phone after telling Turnbull, “It’s the most unpleasant call today.”
