SEOUL, Jan. 9 (Xinhua) -- South Korea and North Korea concluded high-level talks in Panmunjom on the evening of the 9th, and the two sides issued a joint statement agreeing on the DPRK's participation in the Pyeongchang Winter Olympics and the holding of talks between the two military departments.
According to the joint statement issued by the two sides, the DPRK will send a high-level delegation and a delegation of the National Olympic Committee to participate in the Pyeongchang Winter Olympics.
In addition, the DPRK side will also send teams such as athlete groups, cheerleaders, artistic troupes, and press corps to visit South Korea; the Korean side will provide the necessary facilities for this.
The two Koreas also reached an agreement to ease the current military tensions and decided to hold talks between the two military departments.
