According to the report, the per capita purchase volume of foreign tourists is 1.06 million won.
Among them, Chinese tourists have the largest per capita shopping volume of 2.13 million won, 6.5 times that of Japanese tourists, and 3.2 times that of U.S. and European tourists.
When asked about the purpose of visiting Seoul, 62.2% of Chinese tourists answered "shopping" and 94.9% of Chinese tourists bought cosmetics.
96.3 per cent of Chinese tourists shopped at duty-free shops in urban areas, spending 1.56 million won per capita.
