At 7:50 a.m. today (March 10), an explosion occurred at a chemical plant in Xinxiang County, Henan Province, and black smoke was raised at the scene.
The Beijing News reporter learned from the Propaganda Department of the Xinxiang County Party Committee that one person was injured by the explosion.
The video released by local netizens shows that the smoke at the scene of the explosion is billowing, accompanied by noise.
Some netizens said that this morning, the location of the explosion was a chemical factory located in Xiaoji Town, Xinxiang County, Henan Province.
The Beijing News reporter learned that the incident chemical plant is Henan Xinxiang Liutong Industrial Co., Ltd.
According to public information, the above-mentioned enterprises were established in February 2002, and the business scope includes the manufacturing of chemical products.
This afternoon, Xinxiang County Party Propaganda Department responded that the explosion occurred at 7:50 a.m., and the fire has been effectively controlled, and one person has suffered minor injuries. The cause of the incident is under investigation.
The Beijing News reporter noted that as early as 2015, the chemical factory involved was exposed by media, including Henan TV, due to illegal sewage discharge.
On the same day, the director of the original "family suffering", the 85-year-old Yamada worked tirelessly to fly to Beijing and visit the scene in person.
The SFC announced on February 10, 2017 that it approved the initial applications of 12 enterprises in accordance with the statutory procedures on the same day, and asked the above-mentioned enterprises and their underwriters to negotiate with the Shanghai-Shenzhen Stock Exchange to determine the issuance schedule, and successively published prospectus documents.
The reporter of the Beijing Business Daily found that the Guangdong Shangpin Home Home Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Shangpin Housing), which aimed at small and medium-sized boards of the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, ranked among them.
According to the newly announced prospectus, the company was established in 2004, registered in Guangzhou, mainly engaged in the personalized production, sales and sales of supporting home products, and to the home furnishing industry enterprises to provide design software and informatization of overall solutions design, research and development and technical services.
On December 26, the reporter learned from the Municipal Environmental Protection Bureau that in 2012, Lu'an City successfully declared 98 national and provincial environmental protection projects of various types, with a total of 145.26 million yuan in special funds for environmental protection.
Among them, there are 55 national environmental protection projects, striving for 13.246 million yuan of national environmental protection special funds; 43 provincial environmental protection projects, and striving for 12.8 million yuan of special funds for provincial environmental protection.
It is understood that the construction of the project involves the comprehensive management of the regional water environment (including the protection of the ecological environment of the lake), the environmental protection of drinking water sources, the comprehensive rectification of the rural environment, the prevention and control of large-scale livestock and poultry breeding pollution, the pollution control of industrial enterprises, and the demonstration of the construction of ecological cities.
After the implementation of the project, it will play a positive role in promoting the scientific development of the Lu'an City region, realizing the rest and recuperation of lakes, accelerating the improvement of the water environment in the watershed, ensuring the safety of drinking water, and promoting energy conservation and emission reduction.
Today, four groups that have contributed to beautiful China, such as Tonglu County, Zhejiang Province, have won the 8th China Environment Award.
Established in 2000, the Chinese Environment Award is the highest award in the field of environmental protection in China and consists of a selection committee composed of a number of central departments.
Li Wei, head of the selection committee and secretary-general of the China Environmental Protection Foundation, said that China is facing the ecological problems left over from the previous decades of heavy GDP and light environmental protection development model.
The selection of this year's China Environment Award aims to recognize units and individuals who have contributed to improving people's livelihood in order to demonstrate respect for public opinion.
In the view of the selection committee, Tonglu County, Zhejiang Province, based on ecological counties, received this honor.
