July 26th news: On July 22, the reporter learned from the Hongqiao District that the city's city's largest along the river belt park, Hongqiao District South Canal on both sides of the green landscape improvement project was completed and opened to the public free of charge.
With the advantages of the original natural ecology and historical and cultural resources, the entire landscape has been re-planned and upgraded on both sides of the southern canal, creating a five-way landscape along the river in the West Railway Rhythem Corridor of Xintiandi Style Street, Tianzi Jindu Ruins Park.
There are also about 1,500 meters of plastic lanes in the river green area on both sides between Jinhua Bridge and the new three stone bridges, with distance signs placed on them.
In addition to planting a variety of flowers and trees on both sides, a children's playground has also been built, and a number of sculptural sketches have been embellished.
It can be found that the shore has also built seats, roadways, small bridges, hydrophilic platforms and sand pools for children to play, etc., so that cross-strait green landscapes and water systems are integrated, providing the public with another place for leisure, fitness and entertainment.
