President Xi Jinping met with Russian Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev at the Diaoyutai State Guesthouse on November 1.
Xi welcomed Medvedev’s visit to China immediately after his victory at the 19th CPC National Congress, stressing that Russia is China’s biggest neighboring country.
and overall strategic collaborative partners
China's clear goal of developing and deepening China-Russia relations will not change.
China is willing to work with Russia to expand cooperation in various fields and in all aspects, and closely coordinate and cooperate in international affairs.
Promote the building of a community with a shared future for mankind
It is believed that the China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination will seize new opportunities at a new starting point, show new weather and achieve new results.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China and Russia should give full play to the overall coordination role of the prime minister's regular meeting mechanism, and strengthen energy, equipment manufacturing, agriculture, etc.
Cooperation in space and other fields continues to enhance the content of scientific and technological innovation in the cooperation between the two sides, taking the digital economy such as big data, the Internet of Things, and smart cities.
As a new point of cooperation growth
It is necessary to do a good job in docking with the Eurasian Economic Union, strive to promote projects such as coastal international transport corridors, and jointly carry out cooperation in the development and utilization of Arctic waterways.
Building the Ice Silk Road
Promote local exchanges and cooperation between the two countries and further consolidate the public opinion foundation of bilateral relations.
Medvedev conveyed Russian President Vladimir Putin's cordial greetings and good wishes to President Xi Jinping to conclude the victory of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
And Xi Jinping was re-elected as the general secretary of the CPC Central Committee expressed warm congratulations.
More positive progress has been made in cooperation in the fields of economy, energy, investment, innovation, people-to-people and cultural exchanges, and the integration of the Eurasian Economic Union with the Belt and Road construction.
The Russian side is very satisfied with this, and is willing to further strengthen exchanges and cooperation with China in various fields and strengthen communication and coordination in international and regional affairs.
Ding Xuexiang, Yang Jiechi and others participated in the meeting.
Subsequently, the prime ministers of the two countries watched the breakdown.
After the welcoming ceremony, the prime ministers of the two countries co-chaired the 22nd regular meeting between Chinese and Russian prime ministers.
Li Keqiang said that under the impetus of President Xi Jinping and President Putin, China-Russia relations continue to bear new results.
The 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, which has just been successfully concluded.
The election of a new CPC Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping as the core established Xi Jinping's socialist ideology with Chinese characteristics in the new era.
The guiding ideology we must adhere to our party for a long time has clarified China's future development goals.
As the largest developing country, China's development is the basis and key to solving all problems.
China and Russia regard each other's development as an important opportunity.
The two countries are facing broader prospects for docking development strategies and deepening all-round cooperation, and will also contribute more positive forces to peace and development between the two countries, the region and the world.
Li Keqiang and Medvedev listened to the relevant mechanisms of the two countries, Chinese Presidents Zhang Gaoli, Wang Yang and Liu Yandong, as well as the working reports of the Russian chairman.
Create a better tomorrow for bilateral relations.
Medvedev congratulated the Communist Party of China on successfully convening the 19th National Congress, saying that Russia is willing to deepen cooperation with China in traditional fields such as energy, infrastructure construction, production capacity and aerospace.
Expand cooperation in emerging areas such as e-commerce, small and medium-sized enterprises, and strengthen people-to-people and cultural exchanges, so as to promote the continuous development of Russia-China comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination.
After the meeting, Li Keqiang and Medvedev signed the Joint Communiqué of the 22nd Regular Meeting of Chinese and Russian Prime Ministers, and jointly witnessed investment.
Nearly 20 bilateral cooperation documents have been signed in the fields of energy, local cooperation, humanities, agriculture, customs, quality inspection, aerospace and finance.
After the signing ceremony, the prime ministers of the two countries met with reporters and answered questions.
Li Keqiang introduced the results of this meeting, stressing that China is willing to continue to respect each other, equality and mutual benefit.
On the basis of common development, we will promote China-Russia relations and cooperation in various fields, and promote the establishment of a new type of international relations with win-win cooperation as the core.
We also need to create more growth points for cooperation.
It is necessary not only to focus on the advantages of large and strong large enterprises of the two countries, but also to strengthen cooperation in strategic large-scale projects in the fields of energy, aerospace, aviation, and cross-border infrastructure.
Support them to open up new areas of cooperation and accelerate innovation for practical cooperation between the two countries.
In the afternoon of the same day, Li Keqiang and Medvedev jointly attended the closing ceremony of the China-Russia Media Exchange Year and delivered a speech.
He spoke highly of the positive results and social repercussions achieved during the year of media exchanges.
Li Keqiang said in his speech that two years ago, the heads of state of China and Russia jointly decided and announced the launch of the China-Russia Year of media exchanges.
It shows that China and Russia, as comprehensive strategic cooperation partners, have a high degree of mutual trust in politics, are culturally communicative and have an objective and friendly attitude towards each other.
Building important bridges and ties, Li Keqiang pointed out that China and Russia are all countries with long cultural traditions and deep cultural heritage.
The media of the two countries also has their own characteristics.
By holding the year of media exchanges, the two sides have improved understanding, deepened friendship, and promoted mutual learning between the media.
It has become a feature in the history of international media exchanges.
Today's closing ceremony is not the end point, but a new starting point, I believe will open a new chapter of Sino-Russian media cooperation and raise a new sail for people-to-people and cultural exchanges.
Promoting China-Russia relations on a new journey of generational friendship
It gives new connotations to bilateral relations and brings new opportunities, which fully reflects the friendship between the two peoples and the strategic significance of bilateral relations.
