Before closing, Ma Junsheng, director of the State Post Bureau, said in an interview on the "Minister's Channel" that this year, in response to outstanding problems such as courier delays in the current express delivery industry and loss and damage to express shipments, the state will strengthen supervision and guide the strengthening of industry self-discipline.
This year will strengthen efforts to solve the outstanding problems of the four major express delivery industry Ma Junsheng said that the development of China's express delivery industry has now entered the fast lane.
In 2012, China's express delivery volume was 5.6 billion pieces, and 10,000 express three-wheelers were on the road, implementing unified standards, unified logos, and unified insurance, which not only facilitated delivery, but also ensured safety.
