Beijing's "university dredging" new measures: tens of thousands of teachers and students of North chemical industry will be stationed in Changping new campus
The opening ceremony of the new campus of Beijing University of Chemical Technology was held in Changping District of Beijing on the 2nd, and the green campus covering an area of 1,800 acres was officially put into use.
The reporter learned from the ceremony that in order to strengthen the core functions of the capital and manage "big city diseases", in recent years, under the background of Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei collaborative development and relief of non-capital functions, Beijing has accelerated the development of universities in central urban areas to the suburbs, and teachers and students of some universities are gradually moving to new campuses in the suburbs such as Shunyi, Daxing and Fangshan.
Located in Changping Nankou Town, Beijing New Campus covers an area of 1,800 acres and is 40 kilometers away from the city, which is one of the key projects of Beijing's non-capital functions.
The construction of the new campus is divided into three phases, the current first phase of construction has all been completed, the second phase of construction is expected to be fully launched by the end of this year, all completed plans will meet the needs of nearly 20,000 undergraduates, graduate students and teaching staff to study and live.
