The automaker is facing an impact, Audi will modify up to 850,000 diesels
The day before Audi’s announcement, BMW said it would offer software upgrades to more than 350,000 vehicles.
BMW’s chairman said BMW believed there were “more smart options for driving rather than restrictions,” referring to major European cities – including Munich, where the company’s headquarters are located – to consider banning or restricting diesel vehicles.
Daimler on Tuesday announced that it will modify 3 million Mercedes cars in Europe to reduce its diesel emissions.
None of the companies called it a recall.
European automakers have vigorously promoted the use of diesel vehicles in Europe and the United States to help meet carbon dioxide emissions regulations.
However, nitrogen oxides emitted by diesel engines are considered carcinogenic and can cause asthma.
Automotive companies are also installing equipment to offset the cost of diesel exhaust emissions, making it difficult to maintain the competitiveness of diesel cars in terms of price.
As German carmakers face scrutiny, Chancellor Angela Merkel’s government has also been accused of allowing these powerful car companies too much and ignoring signs of the problem.
These car companies are trying to avoid repeating Volkswagen's mistake of masking its use of so-called failed devices, adjusting emissions to comply with regulations while testing cars, and returning to normal under normal driving conditions.
Several VW executives have been charged in the United States, while others are being investigated by countries on both sides of the Atlantic.
Last last month, the former head of thermodynamics in Audi’s engine R&D department was arrested in Germany
Former manager Zachero Giovanni Pamio is Italian and therefore not protected by extradition and may face trial in the United States.
Earlier this year, Audi was embroiled in a German criminal investigation involving VW, and the German government has accused Audi of installing the system to evade European emissions requirements, expanding the scope of previous investigations limited to the United States.
Audi’s investigation is likely to have a significant impact on VW: luxury carmakers account for Volkswagen’s disproportionate share of profits.
From the preparation to the release of a film, it lasted for one or two years or even a few years, which can be described as common.
The animated film "Big Fish" recently announced that it will be released on July 8, and the film lasted 12 years from preparation to release!
The original author of "Big Fish Haitang" Liang Ruo, 21 years old from Tsinghua University's thermal power professional industry, together with his friend Zhang Chun founded the other side, in 2008 won the joint creation of millions of dollars of venture capital, launched the animated film debut "Big Fish Haitang".
The film has won many awards at home and abroad in the creative sample stage, and has also been included and praised as "one of the most outstanding works of art" by the French Centre for Contemporary Art in Pompidou.
Due to six years from creativity to production, the film has been known as the "god's pit" by millions of fans looking forward to the release.
"The Big Fish" tells a fantasy story that belongs to the Chinese people. With the announcement of this scheduled trailer, it brings new expectations to all audiences.
Liang said: "These 12 years have only done this one thing, and now it has changed from a dream to a reality, and I am both nervous and excited."
Zhang Chun said: "I always want to use one-fifth of other people's budgets to make the same picture effect as others, and the team will be driven crazy by me."
