Don't have to look for more than 8000 kinds of products zero tariffs
At the regular press conference held by the Ministry of Commerce on January 11, the spokesman of the Ministry of Commerce said that as of now, there are 15 free trade agreements that have been implemented in China, involving 23 countries and regions, covering more than 8,000 kinds of zero-tariff imported products.
At the same time, imported cosmetics, Icelandic salmon, Chilean red wine, ASEAN tropical fruits... these products don’t have to spend a lot of money.
At present, China has signed 16 free trade agreements with 24 countries and regions, 15 of which have come into effect, covering more than 8,000 kinds of zero-tariff imported products.
Taking agricultural products as an example, with the implementation of free trade agreements, consumers can taste agricultural products from different places of origin, high quality and low price.
For example, tropical fruits such as durians, lychees, and dragon fruit in ASEAN have tariffs ranging from 15% to 30% to zero tariffs.
Icelandic salmon import duties from 10% to 12% reduced to zero tariffs;
Wine imports in Georgia and Chile were reduced from 14% to 30% to zero;
New Zealand's specialty agricultural products such as beef and milk powder have significantly reduced taxes.
Taking industrial products as an example, for example, import tariffs on some cosmetics in Switzerland have been reduced to zero;
The import tariff of some watches has been reduced by 50% and will be reduced to zero after a few years.
South Korea's refrigerators, rice cookers, massagers, beauty machines and other products have been reduced by 40%, and will be reduced to zero tariffs in a few years;
In addition, there are more substantial tax cuts in consumer electronic products.
At the same time, the zero-tariff products under the free trade zone also include the intermediate products and raw materials required for the manufacturing of many domestic end consumer goods, and also promote the structural upgrading of domestic consumer goods to a certain extent.
The spokesman of the Ministry of Commerce said that nearly one-third of China's total imports of products can enjoy preferential tariffs on free trade agreements, most of which are terminal consumer goods, which has brought real benefits to consumers.
Further reduction of import tariffs on consumer goods
Since December 1, 2017, China's import tariffs on some consumer goods have been adjusted to further reduce import tariffs on consumer goods, covering various types of consumer goods such as food, health care products, pharmaceuticals, daily necessities, clothing, shoes and hats, household equipment, culture and entertainment, and grocery stores, involving a total of 187 8-bit tax numbers.
The average tax rate for these consumer goods will be reduced from 17.3 percent to 7.7 percent, which will almost be cut off!
Since January 1, 2018, China has also made partial adjustments to other import and export tariffs.
The import tariffs on some cosmetics such as lip balms, eyes, and perfumes have been reduced from 10% to 5%;
After reducing tariffs, it means that consumers don't have to buy on their behalf, and they don't have to run abroad to buy their favorite foreign products.
