Foreign reports: at the end of the year, the U.S. shopping mall stipulates that there is a big difference, and shopping returns need to be careful
The new network on December 29th.
According to the U.S. "World Daily" reported that just after Christmas, ushered in the tide of returns.
According to ABC, more than half of the goods sold last Christmas were returned.
In addition, some readers have repeatedly revealed that online shopping has been cheated, and consumers need to pay more attention when shopping on informal websites.
In general, large shopping companies have regular and reasonable return procedures, but if you buy gifts or e-commerce shopping from some small stores, you must be careful.
On December 1st local time, Ms. Hou of Rolangong bought a jacket for more than 60 yuan (US dollars, the same below) at an online shop that specializes in printing jackets, and it has not been sent until now.
She sent an e-mail and did not reply.
Other netizens broke the news that they went to the United States last year, bought a mobile phone from third-party sellers, and found that there was a box of plaster inside.
After knowing that you have been cheated, apply for a refund from the website and get a full refund.
However, some customers believe that the website refund service is not 100% perfect.
Mr. Wang, a Chinese resident of Northern California, said that he had twice purchased an expedited delivery service for a website, an expedited service of four yuan, but two times it was not delivered on time.
After that, I applied for a refund and did not receive a response.
Large shopping malls or shopping malls have better return policies.
Macy’s has a full refund within 180 days.
However, the goods must remain "original" and must have purchase vouchers such as receipts or bank purchase records.
If there is no certificate, the customer can also get market points, which can be used to purchase other goods.
Target usually has a 90-day return period for general goods, and electronic products usually have 15 days.
However, from November 1 to December 25, 2017, the return period for electronic and entertainment products purchased was extended to 30 days.
It should be noted that the 30-day refund period starts from December 25, that is, it must be returned before January 25, 2018.
The ultimate shopping experience, the new era of shopping development in the business district is coming
More than a decade ago, China is still in the seller's market in general, and people's choices are limited and demand is limited.
However, after ten years of development, the market has already realized the transformation from the seller's market to the buyer's market, and today's consumer tastes have become more and more, and they are no longer satisfied with the simple "one-handed delivery" shopping behavior.
Therefore, how to let consumers get an extreme shopping experience has become the next competition for real estate developers.
Among the many factors that affect the shopping experience of consumers, shopping centers in the business district have the most significant impact.
Look at how city builders pay attention to the shopping experience.
There are no two identical leaves in the world, and there are not two shopping centers that are exactly the same, and a famous shopping center must have its own characteristics.
For example, Turkey's world-famous Kanyon shopping center, its unique wavy architectural design inspired by the Grand Canyon (Canyon), so named homophonic Kanyon, walking in Kanyon's 200-meter walk seems to be inside the Grand Canyon.
In addition to the canyon design, there is also a large oval performance venue in the middle of the shopping center, with a unique appearance, which will often hold special performances.
Because of the open platform design, visitors can walk on each floor to see the activities carried out by the "canyon", and have the effect of shifting scenery.
In China, Nanjing Forest Moore Commercial Street, known as China's first forest-style stroll consumption field, perfectly combines shopping with ecology and fairy tales.
7000 square meters of green space square, 3000 square meters of rooftop water platform, the project consists of 9 single buildings, the air corridors between each building, the overall sinking courtyard design, take the French sycamore trees on the ground for the epidermis of the building, the roof of the water platform, to create a forest-like feeling.
Walking into the forest mooles is like accidentally falling into the rabbit hole in Alice's roaming adventures, climbing along the trunk to surround the building, the meadows, the springs against each other, bringing people into a forest full of vitality and vitality.
Also in Chongqing, Longhu to build Lijia water business district, planning Baifang business, plans to introduce more than 50 international top monopoly flagship stores in the future, more than 100 international top brands and more than 500 domestic and foreign famous brands, to become a service industry agglomeration, the theme of distinctive characteristics of the commercial center.
Not only that, Liejia water business district will also integrate the ecology into the building, TOD public transportation-oriented, set fashion shopping, life services, catering, entertainment, education, sports in one, to bring consumers the ultimate shopping experience while also leading them to enjoy Chongqing's unique "waterfront culture", shopping and water entertainment, leisure perfect integration.
In summary, it can be found that at present, some real estate companies have gained insight into the discovery trajectory of this new urban business, and industry insiders said that this consumption model centered on consumer experience and how to combine shopping and experience will also be the mainstream of future urban development.
Today's business district is not only the distribution center of goods, but also a comprehensive place that integrates artistic culture and creative theme, and also carries people's responsibilities for urban living.
Therefore, while meeting the one-stop material needs of consumers, maximizing the spiritual needs of culture and art, and giving play to the livable housing needs, it will inevitably be the commanding heights for the future development of the business district.
In Chongqing, Guoxing's northern shore Jiangshan, located in Jiangbei, close to Guanyin Bridge, the world's commercial essence, the left and right of the international giants, first-class brands gathered together to connect with international fashion.
Here, step by step, the essence of the world;
Dongyuan Jinyue has a better shopping environment, Dongyuan Jinyue is close to Nanping business district, exclusive to the west and even the country's leading four-story three-dimensional transportation system, enhance shopping comfort.
In addition, the landscaping and landscape paving of the two pedestrian streets of Huigong Road and Wanda Square have been upgraded, about 300 trees have been planted, 40,000 square meters have been renovated, which has improved the image of Nanping Business District;
And Longhu Yuhu, near Chongqing's first low-density waterfront business district - Lijia waterfront business district, is surrounded by nine parks, the commercial district has a low density and a high degree of openness, so that people are more willing to stay, stop, and slowly enjoy the fun of shopping when shopping, rather than being rushed forward by the people behind, and truly realize "walking shopping".
Today's business competition will only become more and more fierce, how to kill a bloody road in a homogenized market, won the reputation of the future consumer's heart of the "shopping shrine", worthy of all real estate developers to seriously think about.
Only relying on the differentiation strategy is not enough, only those who really put consumers in their hearts, anxious consumers, want consumers to think, to provide consumers with the ultimate and simple shopping experience of the developers in the tempest of the market.
Of course, in the end, I think the people of Chongqing, who have such a good shopping experience and business circle, were placed 10 years ago, and no one could have imagined today's prosperity.
Festival of Things: Consumerism Orchid Covers Real Environmental Prices
168.2 billion yuan, this is November 11, 2017, "Tmall double eleven global carnival" within 24 hours, Tmall users consume turnover.
Specifically, after the start of "Double 11", Tmall's turnover exceeded 10 billion yuan in just 3 minutes, more than 20 billion yuan in 6 minutes and 05 seconds, and 100 billion yuan in 9 hours.
On this day, the total number of payments completed by global consumers through Alipay reached 1.48 billion, an increase of 41% over last year.
These purchases will result in 812 million logistics orders.
Whether it is Tmall online shopping platform or Alipay payment platform, it all belongs to Ma Yun's Ali Group.
Ten years ago, no one would have thought that on November 11th, the "Singles Day" sub-culture created by the single youth out of self-deprecation will be compiled by e-commerce, which has become today's phenomenal "double 11" shopping carnival.
On November 11, 2009, Alibaba for the first time used the marketing gimmick of "Singles Day promotion": no one fell in love with you, then the "single dogs" came to the online shopping bar.
The results were surprising, and on this day, the transaction volume of Taobao Mall ("Tmall's predecessor") exceeded 52 million yuan, which was 10 times that of daily transactions at that time.
Since then, "double 11" has become a shopping carnival created by Alibaba, from the beginning of the domestic buyers and sellers to entertain themselves, and now the influx of global merchants, nine years later, Tmall "double 11" 100 billion transactions have been more than 3,200 times of that year, so that "Black Friday" can't wait.
With the trend Tmall "double eleven" promotion, there are many e-commerce companies, of which "Jingdong" is the most powerful.
"Jingdong" has its own shopping festival "6.18", but there is no "double 11" has a big impact, this year from November 1 to the 11th, Jingdong cumulative sales reached 127.1 billion yuan.
After the "double 11", it is followed by a similar "double 12" discount carnival, Christmas and New Year shopping schedule.
Crossing the New Year, waiting for Chinese consumers, there is also the purchase schedule before the Spring Festival, Valentine's Day shopping schedule, consumption, will not take a vacation.
The environmental problems brought about by the instantaneous mass consumption have attracted the attention of professionals and institutions.
According to the Xinhua Daily Telegraph, according to the usual standard of 0.2 kilograms per box in the industry, at least 300,000 tons of garbage were generated during this year's "double 11" period.
Liu Hua, director of the pollution prevention and control project of Greenpeace East Asia Division, told China and foreign dialogue that this year's "double 11" only Tmall's orders will produce 160,000 tons of packaging waste.
According to a report issued by the State Post Office in 2016, it pointed out that during the "double 11" period in 2015 (November 11 to 16), there were about 780 million express shipments, using more than 3 billion woven bags, 9.922 billion boxes, 16.985 billion meters of tape, the length of the tape can circle the Earth's equator 425 times.
This year, the National Postal Administration expects "double 11" express business volume is expected to exceed 1.5 billion pieces.
Wang Shi, manager of a garbage incineration center in Beijing, told Xinhua News Agency that more than 2,000 tons of garbage entered every day after "double 11", which also exceeded the processing capacity of incineration stations.
The express delivery company has realized that the environmental pollution caused by the express delivery industry cannot be looked at.
Some e-commerce logistics companies, including Suning, "double 11" before the introduction of recyclable and re-usable plastic courier boxes, can be reused as shopping bags and garbage bags of circulating bags, etc., but troublesome consumer acceptance is not high.
Ma also called on the logistics industry to support "green packaging" and "green logistics".
