"New retail" that has been enchanted.
Chen Yilei and Yang Kaihan: Amazon announced its entry into bookstores and groceries stores when squeezed into the world's top ten retailers, regardless of timing or motivation.
In November 2015, Amazon opened its first brick-and-mortar bookstore in Seattle, followed by two bookstores in Portland and San Diego.
At the beginning of 2017, Amazon opened stores in New York and planned to have at least eight stores by the end of the year.
At almost the same time, Amazon announced that its unmanned supermarket (Amazon Go) trial operation, customers to the store do not need queuing, also do not need checkout, into the door scan code, take the desired goods to leave, the purchase amount will be automatically deducted from the customer's Amazon account.
As far as Amazon is concerned, in recent years, it is a very unexpected thing to suddenly move frequently on physical stores.
Because as early as 2007's "open letter to shareholders", CEO Jeff Bezos stressed that Amazon will not easily open a physical store, unless the following four conditions are met at the same time:
We must be convinced that this new opportunity will allow shareholders to return on their investments.
We must be convinced that this new opportunity is of great significance to the company as a whole;
We must be convinced that this new opportunity is ignored by the market.
We must be convinced that in this market, we have sufficient resources to differentiate our customers.
Bookshops and grocery stores are the most shaky categories in both brick-and-mortar retailers, as well as Amazon’s first rivals to fall.
When Amazon squeezed into the world's top ten retailers, it announced its entry into these two physical markets, regardless of timing or motivation.
Is Amazon's approach contrary to the guarantees contained in the shareholders' letter?
A similar voice was heard on the other side of the globe. On the morning of October 13, 2016, at the 2016 Hangzhou Yunqi Conference, Ma Yun, chairman of Alibaba's board of directors, delivered a keynote speech.
He said: "Starting next year, Alibaba will no longer talk about 'e-commerce,'" he said.
The era of pure e-commerce will soon end, and there will be no e-commerce in the next ten or twenty years, replaced by "new retail".
The combination of online and offline and logistics will lead to new retail.”
For a time, the three words of "new retail" seemed to have been enchanted, and they were frequently used by people in the industry.
But what does “new retail” mean?
If it is just a combination of online and offline, then this concept is not new.
In 2016, eMarketer, after tracking 180 of the largest e-commerce companies, estimated that the total e-commerce sales were about $200 billion, and the 25 largest accounted for more than $159 billion.
Of these 25, 18 are traditional retailers (such as Macy's, Nordstrom, Target, Gap, etc.), which have only been operating online in the past five years.
Alibaba Group's 28.3 billion yuan of shares in Suningyun merchants is also vivid.
From a global perspective, retailers and e-commerce are moving from a single channel to an omni-channel retail system that covers physical stores, e-commerce, mobile and social media.
Is Ma Yun talking about "new retail", which is more of a summary than a vision for the future?
If not, then the concept of omnichannel, what is the difference from "new retail"?
Perhaps, the key to the problem is not whether online and offline will be integrated, but how to integrate.
Looking back at the past 20 years in the retail industry, the rise of e-commerce, like the rise of early discount retailers, is focused on price and convenience.
Relying on these two pain points, e-commerce has moved highly standardized products, such as books and CDs, from offline to online.
With the development of online consumption habits and the continuous improvement of customer experience, e-commerce has extended its tentacles to other categories and begun to improve efficiency.
In the words of Alibaba CEO Zhang Yong, “Using the ideas and technology of the Internet to comprehensively reform and upgrade the existing total of about 30 trillion social retailers, so that the escalating consumer demand of Chinese consumers can be effectively met, making the whole process of commodity production, circulation and services more efficient because of the extensive use of the Internet and big data.”
Therefore, the road of e-commerce is a road of light assets on the surface and actual heavy assets.
"Light" refers to the burden of fixed assets, staffing, management processes, etc. There is no traditional retail size; "heavy" refers to the need for huge investment in logistics, warehousing and other aspects.
The change of logistics methods ensures the high efficiency of e-commerce.
According to the Chinese government website, Premier Li Keqiang chaired the executive meeting of the State Council on April 28, at which he believed that expanding domestic consumer demand was an important measure to stabilize growth and adjust the structure.
The meeting determined that the relevant departments should urgently come up with specific plans on the basis of scientific evaluation.
For some foreign daily consumer goods with high domestic consumer demand, the pilot reduction of import tariffs will be carried out by the end of June this year, and the scope of tariff reduction goods will be gradually expanded;
Combined with the reform of the tax system, improve the consumption tax policy of mass consumer goods such as clothing and cosmetics, and comprehensively adjust the scope of taxation, tax rates and collection links;
Increase and restore port entry duty-free shops, rationally expand duty-free varieties, increase a certain number of duty-free purchases, and facilitate domestic consumers to purchase foreign products in China;
We will further promote the facilitation of overseas passengers' shopping customs clearance and tax refunds, and strictly implement the tax return requirements for imported goods in accordance with the law.
Develop inspection and quarantine policies to support cross-border e-commerce imports, and clean up unreasonable charges for import links;
Accelerating the promotion of China's product brand upgrading projects, supporting the development of physical stores, and realizing online and offline interaction.
Regulate the market order, severely fight counterfeiting, and promote the survival of the fittest.
Let consumers be able to be comfortable and convenient shopping.
