On January 18, Alibaba held an e-commerce poverty alleviation peak dialogue meeting in Chongqing, announcing that through the exploration of a new model of "Internet + poverty alleviation" to promote accurate poverty alleviation and rural revitalization.
After proposing rural strategies, launching rural Taobao projects, launching agricultural poverty alleviation platforms, and setting up Alibaba's poverty alleviation fund, Ali once again "increased weight" in the fight against poverty.
Poverty alleviation is one of China's most important national strategies.
Full eradication of poverty has not been achieved in China for thousands of years.
"E-commerce poverty alleviation is an innovative measure for a new round of poverty alleviation and development, and it is an important starting point to achieve accurate poverty alleviation and accurate poverty alleviation."
The central government attaches great importance to and points out that it can give full play to the role of the Internet in promoting poverty alleviation, promoting accurate poverty alleviation, precision poverty alleviation, and allowing agricultural products to walk out of the countryside through the Internet.”
Therefore, as early as 2014, Ali put forward a rural strategy, which is listed as Ali's three core strategies in the next 20 years, along with big data cloud computing and globalization.
In the same year, Ali launched the rural Taobao (village Tao) project to recruit "village two" in the countryside and lead farmers to get rid of poverty through e-commerce.
In 2017, Ali cooperated with the business department to build an agricultural poverty alleviation channel, and currently has a total of 13 provinces and 120 national poverty-stricken counties across the country.
There are already 2,118 Taobao villages spawned by Ali platforms.
Among them, nearly 400 appeared in poverty-stricken prefectures in the provinces, and 33 in poverty-stricken counties in 13 countries.
In 2017, on Alibaba's Chinese retail platform, Taobao Village's sales reached 120 billion yuan.
Zhang Yong said that in the face of the national strategy of poverty alleviation, Ali has been thinking about how to make good use of Ali's economy's innovation capabilities such as science and technology, big data, and cloud computing, so as to take a new way out of poverty.
Among them, Village Tao is the main carrying platform for Ali e-commerce to get rid of poverty, and walked through a new Internet poverty alleviation link directly for direct sales.
In the planting process, the village and ant financial service jointly carried out agricultural tools and small loan support.
In 2017, among the 832 state-level poverty-stricken prefectures, Ant Financial served 795, providing them with convenient payment, credit and other services.
Cainiao solves warehousing and logistics, Tmall is responsible for sales, and Aliyun's big data guides agricultural production to further improve the supply standards, quality and market competitiveness of agricultural products.
The development of e-commerce out of poverty requires not only products, sales channels, and industrial planning, but also talents.
Through Taobao University, Ali opened e-commerce courses to teach farmers standardized, quality and large-scale planting methods, and realized the combination of "poverty alleviation + supporting the mind", so that farmers can get rid of poverty sustainably.
These courses already cover about 92 per cent of state-level poverty-stricken counties.
The idea of "public welfare mentality and commercial means" to get rid of poverty can also ensure that Ali can achieve "true poverty alleviation" in poverty alleviation.
Ma Yun, chairman of Alibaba's board of directors, said that the eradication of poverty should be divided into three stages: poverty alleviation, poverty alleviation, and getting rich.
Poverty alleviation is to teach people to fish, poverty alleviation is to teach people to fish, wealth is to create a "fish pond" for farmers, so that farmers have fish to raise.
The industrial poverty alleviation driven by e-commerce is to make fish ponds.
In terms of industrial poverty alleviation, the Luochuan apple industry poverty alleviation model created by Ali in cooperation with Luochuan, Shaanxi, has been copied and promoted by the relevant departments as an example throughout the country.
Ali e-commerce poverty alleviation work has also been recognized by the decision-making level.
The e-commerce companies represented by Alibaba have been sent messages to ensure that farmers increase production and income through online and offline channels.
A number of villagee and ants are also invited to the United Nations and Africa to share the experience of e-commerce out of poverty.
At present, the China office of the United Nations World Food Programme has carried out poverty alleviation in the e-commerce industry in Anhui and other places.
The "Third New Economic Think Tank Conference" co-organized by the Ali Research Institute and the China Foresight Think Tan was held on January 16, and Zhang Li, director of the e-commerce institute of the Research Institute of the Ministry of Commerce, attended and spoke.
She believes that our globalization actually ignores the most important issues, that is, the physical and useful problems of globalization, as well as the stage of globalization.
In this way, many people think that globalization has stagnated, and many developed and developing countries, in the new stage, their attitude towards globalization is not the same, is different from the model.
The second concept is the problem in the middle stage of globalization, and what are the constraints of the middle stage of globalization?
Due to the constraints on the basis of the economic environment, it is precisely because the economic foundation has changed that globalization has been restricted.
Zhang Li believes that at the end of 2017, the global economic adjustment is basically over, and after 2018, it will enter a new round of growth, and the next round of growth must be driven by raw products.
