In order to optimize the environment of the scenic spot and build a beautiful Nanyue, recently, the "636" volunteer service team of Nanyue District Tobacco Special Bureau (branch) has carried out environmental protection activities of "climbing forests and protecting homes".
The activities not only received the support of all the cadres and employees of the District Tobacco Bureau, but also attracted retired old cadres and the families of employees to participate in environmental protection practices, and the three generations of old and young people worked together to protect forests, clean up the garbage, and contributed their own strength to the construction of "beautiful South".
This volunteer service activity is designed to protect Nanyue's scenic resources, carry forward the concept of "caring for others, caring for society, caring for nature", and allowing the next generation to accept edification from childhood and inherit the virtues of voluntary service.
It is reported that since the establishment of the "636" volunteer service team at the beginning of April this year, a total of 16 members have been developed, and have carried out a series of voluntary service activities such as visiting disabled retail customers, helping tobacco farmers to care for tobacco leaves, Ya'an earthquake love donations, and becoming a voluntary volunteer force that conveys positive energy.
