Does meat, dairy products, and chocolate help relieve inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)?
The meat and chocolate may sound like a nightmare for your digestive system.
But a new study shows the exact opposite: a meat-rich diet rich in proteins and dairy products can help relieve symptoms associated in patients with inflammatory bowel disease.
The incurable disease, which affects about 1.3 million Americans and about 300,000 Britons, has a life impact, resulting in stomach cramps and bloating, recurrent or haemorrhagic diarrhoea, weight loss and extreme fatigue.
Researchers at the University of Washington usually recommend that patients avoid eating meat and dairy products to relieve symptoms, but researchers have found that the protein’s key amino acid, tryptophan, helps promote immune cell growth, and that these cells can improve the tolerance of the gut.
Lead researcher Dr Marco Colonna explained that immune cells patrol the intestines to ensure that harmful microbes hidden in food don’t sneak into their bodies.
Maintain a balance between the cells that cause inflammation and the cells that promote tolerance, protecting the body without damaging all kinds of sensitive and fragile tissues.
When the equilibrium state is too biased towards inflammation, inflammatory bowel disease may occur.
In the experiment, it was found that an immune-promoting cell appeared in mice carrying special bacteria.
Bacteria require tryptophan (one of the components of a protein) to form the appearance of cells.
Professor Colonna said: "We have established a link between a bacterial population (Lactobacteria Royce, which is a normal part of the gut microbiota) and a cell population that promotes tolerability.
The more tryptophone mice consume in their diet, the more immune cells they have.
He suggested that if humans used the same approach, i.e., a combination of Lactobacillus Lucill and tryptophan-rich diets, it might form a more tolerant and less inflammatory gut environment.
Postdoctoral researcher Luisa Cervantes-Barraganwas, who studied an immune cell that improves tolerability, didn’t do it when she discovered that one group of studied mice had such cells, but the other set of the same strains were raised separately.
She suspects that this difference is related to the gut microbiome of mice (referring to the communities of bacteria, viruses, and fungi that usually live within the gastrointestinal tract).
DNA-sequencing the cholesterol of mice revealed that there were six bacterial populations present in mice with immune cells, but not in mice without immune cells.
Rats are raised in sterile environments, so they lack gut microbes, and they can't show up with this immune cell, and Lactobacillus lutteria produces immune cells.
To understand how bacteria affect the immune system, the researchers cultured Lactobacillus Lucill in liquids and then transferred small amounts of bacterium-free liquids to immature immune cells isolated from mice.
This immune cell develops into a tolerant cell.
When the active ingredient is purified from the liquid, it can be proved that the active ingredient is a by-product of tryptophan metabolism, known as indoe-3-lactic acid.
When the researchers doubled the number of tryptophans in mouse feed, the number of such cells increased by about 50 percent, but by the halving of tryptophan levels, the number of cells had been halved.
Dr. Cervantes-Barragan explained that people, like mice, have cells that have the same tolerance, and most of us have Lactobacillus luttellus in our gastrointestinal tract.
It is not known whether humans, like mice in experiments, can induce tryptophin byproducts from Lactobacterius in their bodies to induce cell development, but genetic defects related to tryptophan are found in patients with inflammatory bowel disease.
She said: "The development of these cells may be exactly what we want, because these cells can control the inflammatory response on the surface of the gut."
It’s not true that the presence of high levels of tryptophan in lactobacterium lutteria may lead to an increase in the number of these strains.
Jose Mourinho thinks Manchester United have signed 'genius' Nemania Matić
On Wednesday night, after Neymania Matici made his debut in the Sampdolia rivalry, Mourinho determined that Manchester United had signed a "genius" midfielder.
Matic, from Chelsea, signed for up to £40m, playing 2-1 in the final pre-season of the Europa Super Cup against Real Madrid on Tuesday, winning the favour of Paul Pogba and Andreas Pereira.
However, in the Blues pre-season Asian Tour, Matic's performance was woefully deficient, with only 45 minutes completed, with Mourinho acknowledging that improvements were needed before the Premier League season began.
“He needs time, but he has experience, wisdom and a genius way of thinking – he thinks about football,” Mourinho said.
"We're going to help him get ready as soon as possible."
Jose Mourinho started his starting line-up at the beginning of the same season. Like Matic, new signings Victor Lindelof and Romelu Lukaku have also started their games at Aviva Stadium.
Jose Mourinho still wants to bring in three more signing players, he reported this week, but he insists the club "did a great job" and he has four preferred signing players in his mind, three of whom have been brought in by the club.
“The club brought in three of them, and I’m very grateful,” he added.
"I'd be happier if the club were able to bring in all four players, but they've done a lot for me."
Will China lag behind if it doesn't build this type of warship?
As the world's major naval powers have recently announced the construction plan of new frigates, it seems that overnight frigates have become the focus of naval attention of major powers, first Japan in the 2018 annual defense budget to determine the purchase of two new frigates, so that Japan's DEX frigate plan finally had a substantial breakthrough, then the United States Lockheed Martin recently announced the latest plan of the United States FFG frigate plan, then China's new frigate where to go?
With the launch of the latest 054A frigate at the end of 2017, it marks that as many as 29 054A frigates have been built, and they have been close to the sum of 053H series frigates, and since the launch of the first 054A in 2006, the construction process of 054A has been completed for 12 years, even in the world, the construction of such a large number of high-performance general-purpose frigates, in addition to China, only the "Perry"-class frigate built by the United States in the 1970s.
And the reason why we want to build so many 054As is also very simple, that is, affordable, easy to use, plus supplement for many years of naval debts.
054A frigate with a high cost performance and good combat ability has been favored by the Chinese Navy for many years, its displacement of about 4000 tons, equipped with a 76 mm main gun, 32 units of sea red flag-16 and fish-8 anti-submarine missile common launch system, 8 hawk 83 and a straight -9 helicopter, although it began to build in 2006, the design time is a kind of ship, but its combat effectiveness even today is not too bad.
However, after all, this is a type of 21st century designed ships, the weapon configuration aside, its power system and electronic radar equipment compared with the current world's mainstream frigates there is already a big gap, such as Europe's same type of frigates have been equipped with all-electric propulsion, small multifunctional phased array radars, large-scale helicopter decks, it is also time to develop a new model.
So how China's new frigates should be developed is directly related to its future positioning and our Chinese navy's strategic approach.
The future development of China's navy will surely become a blue-water navy, and the future will also go to the ocean, with areas closely related to China's vital interests for rapid deployment, showing the existence of force, if necessary, to have a strong combat power to ensure that China's vital interests in the region will not be damaged, so it seems that the new Hu Wei River will be towards large-scale and oceanic development.
Looking at the positioning of the new frigates in China's naval sequence in the future, the Chinese navy in the future should be similar to the U.S. Navy, in addition to the necessary offshore defense ships, the other main ships will be based on the needs of the situation to form an aircraft carrier battle group or amphibious assault ship strike group.
The role of the new frigate in the future aircraft carrier battle group should act as the anti-submarine main force and the positioning of the hollow and near-periment area, in the amphibious assault ship strike group should act as an escort ship class, then according to such needs requires that the new frigate must have a strong anti-submarine capability and a good medium-range area release capability.
Based on the above positioning, you can boldly imagine the approximate appearance of domestic frigates in the future.
First of all, there will be a substantial increase in the displacement relative to the current 054A frigate, and it is estimated that the displacement of the new frigate will reach about 5000-6000 tons; the power system will use an integrated electric propulsion system consisting of an QC280 improved gas turbine and two diesel engines, the maximum speed is expected to reach about 30 knots, and the endurance will also be greatly increased; as for the weapon configuration of the 76 mm main cannon and 1130 near-contamination, it should be retained.
In this way, the overall level of the new frigates will reach the current first-class level in the world, even if compared with the FFG of the United States.
Of course, the above concept is only the author's conjecture about the domestic new frigate, how can we only wait until the new frigate is launched, let's look forward to it together.
(Makarov)
(Compilation/Feng Xue)
