According to the market star, from 2005 to 2011, our province's GDP was tied from the "bottom of the middle" to the second place.
However, there are still difficulties such as low investment efficiency and lack of core competitiveness of the industrial economy. To this end, the latest issue of the Provincial Economic Information Center's "Economic Blue Pages" proposes to improve the quality and efficiency of economic growth.
On the basis of some representative indicators of the province's economy in 2005 and 2011, it was compared with the whole country and the central region.
In terms of industrial economic benefits, in 2011, high energy-consuming industries such as industrial energy and raw materials, which occupy a considerable proportion in our province, are greatly affected by market fluctuations and "double pressure" of overcapacity, and at the same time, the innovation of leading industries such as home appliances and automobiles is insufficient, resulting in meager profits.
A large amount of investment has not brought corresponding economic benefits, which is an important reason for the low quality and efficiency of our province's economic growth.
In this regard, experts suggest that effective measures should be taken to encourage enterprise innovation, and the scientific and technological achievements of universities and scientific research institutes should also be "transferred" to enterprises in a timely manner.
For industrial economic benefits are not high, experts said that we should also actively promote the merger and reorganization of the industry, optimize the industrial layout, and extend the industrial chain.
