La Liga may regret throwing an olive branch on Marko Villatti
Paris Saint-Germain won't give up on signing Neymar after making a £189m offer to try to exercise its exemption, but did they warn Barcelona three years ago to launch an attack on the World Records Raider?
This sensational approach has opened the summer transfer window, with Ligue 1 clubs ready to break the world's transfer record for more than twice the previous transfer record. Paul Pogba returned to Manchester United last season, amounting to £89 million.
Once completed, Neymar will become the world's highest-priced player and the world's highest-paid professional athlete, Paris Saint-Germain, to provide more than £500,000 per week in after-tax pay.
Barcelona was outraged by Neymar’s offensive approach and the way out, and sources familiar with Catalonia’s board insisted that after his arrival from Santos in 2013, the club had gone to great lengths to take care of him.
But did Paris Saint-Germain’s president make such predictions about the world of football three years ago?
When Manchester City expressed interest in signing Bryce Matedi in 2014, Nasser al-Ghlefi issued a stern warning to any club that wanted to sign Paris Saint-Germain's best player.
“I’m not worried because they know that if they touch any of our players, we’re going to confront them and we’re going to contact their players as well,” Alkhlefi said.
