Wang Yichen, a reporter of this newspaper, reported that the international seminar on new energy development and technology jointly sponsored by the national power grid company and the International Electrotechnical Commission was recently held in Frankfurt, Germany.
At present, accelerating the development of new energy and promoting the clean and low-carbon transformation of energy has become a global trend.
The large-scale development and utilization of new energy, as well as system safety problems, long-distance transmission problems, technical and economic problems and many other problems and challenges need to be faced and solved.
Shu Yibiao, chairman of the State Grid Corporation, revealed that the State Grid Corporation is planning to expand the synchronous grid scale, strengthen the interconnection of the existing regional power grid, and increase the cross-regional transmission capacity to about 300 million kilowatts by 2020.
