January 3: The reporter learned yesterday from the Guangzhou Municipal Flower City Office that the Springflower Market in 2008 will start bidding in the near future.
On the 29th and 30th of last month, the bidding for the orange and flower positions were carried out respectively.
Yuexiu District Archives is organizing and collecting hundreds of old photos of the historic Spring Festival City (which is 50 or 60 years old), scheduled to hold a public exhibition at the Yuexiu District Culture and Art Center on January 8, 2008, when the flower market began to build at the end of January, these old photos will be moved to the Beijing Road Guangbai Square for the exhibition.
In addition, Yuexiu District Cultural Bureau will also hold a flower market forum, inviting Guangzhou's old leaders, social folk experts, social celebrities, and old neighbors of Beijing Road to talk about the history and future development of Beijing Road West Lake Road.
At that time, the flower market forum will contact the online media for online live broadcasting and interact with the public simultaneously.
In addition, it has also opened an online flower market, using the community information network to send an introduction text message about the flower market to the citizens who entered the Beijing Road Business District and the West Lake Road Flower Market, and could use their mobile phones to browse the "online flower market".
