LONDON, Jan. 9 (Xinhua) -- The British Sports Council announced on the 9th that its goal to participate in South Korea's Pyeongchang Winter Olympics next month is to win at least five medals, which is "the most ambitious" goal in the history of the British delegation's participation in the Winter Olympics.
The British Sports Council is responsible for the allocation of funds for various Olympic projects and, of course, is responsible for issuing winning targets for various projects.
It is estimated that British athletes have the hope of impacting medal projects from snowboarding, curling, steel frame snowmobiles and short track speed skating and so on.
In the past Winter Olympics cycle, the British Sports Council allocated a total of 32 million pounds (about 280 million yuan) of training funds for the Winter Olympic Games project, and the cycle of the Posiche Winter Olympic Games has doubled.
Most of the money comes from the National Lottery, and the rest comes from state finances.
Britain's hopes of winning gold are mainly pinned on the two, one is Alice Christie, the three gold medalists of last year's world short track speed skating championships, and the other is the last women's steel frame snowmobile champion Liz Arnold.
At the Sochi Winter Olympics in 2014, the British delegation achieved a record of 1 gold, 1 silver and 2 copper, which was their best record since the first Winter Olympics in 1924.
